That is the very idea that I started with, too (as evidenced by still
more startscumming).  The problem that I ran into with a monk was not
having hungerless casting.  Without the food from eating corpses,
inventory food, and death drops, I started to run low on food because
of the spell casting.  Furthermore, engraving Elbereth was less likely
to succeed because of the lower starting Int.  I'm not sure if it was
operator error or a true difference in the roles, but I just seemed to
have a much easier time avoiding food issues in the early game (and
then not having to kill soldiers for food in the mid-late game) with a
wizard than with a monk despite being able to zap 'sleep' as a monk
and only (assuming no great second spell) having good odds at dusting
Elbereth as a wizard.  Perhaps things would have changed if I had
survived longer, though.



